Next, we're diving into skills, more specifically, how to create and use skills inside of Claude.

763
01:02:45,424 --> 01:02:50,384
你可以在 Claude 的网页版中创建技能，甚至可以在那里上传它们。
You can create skills inside of the Claude web version, and you can even upload them there.

764
01:02:50,544 --> 01:02:58,500
但再次强调，这些功能不如在 Cowork 中强大，因为 Cowork 可以直接访问你的电脑，它可以运行脚本，
But again, they're not as powerful as when you do this inside of Cowork because Cowork has direct access to your computer, it can run scripts,

765
01:02:58,704 --> 01:03:05,184
而且在执行这些技能并为你创建它们时，它能调用的工具也多得多。
and overall it has many more tools that are available to it when it's executing those skills and creating them for you.

766
01:03:05,454 --> 01:03:06,224
什么是技能？
What is a skill?

767
01:03:06,384 --> 01:03:12,544
嗯，技能基本上是一个可重复的过程，你可以让 Claude 每次都以同样的方式去执行。
Well, a skill is basically a repeatable process that you can have Claw do the same way every single time.

768
01:03:12,718 --> 01:03:19,424
它会遵循那个逐步的工作流，使用你已经定义好的工具，从而创建一个你可以始终信任的可靠工作流，
It goes through that step-by-step workflow, uses tools that you've already defined, and it creates a reliable workflow that you can always trust

769
01:03:19,758 --> 01:03:23,664
这样你就不用每次回到对话框里，让它每次都以不同的方式去操作了。
so that you're not just going back into the chat and it's doing it differently every single time.

770
01:03:23,950 --> 01:03:29,764
有了技能，你就能获得同样的约束条件、同样的过程、同样的工具，所有这些都能保持高度一致。
With a skill, you get the same guardrails, the same process, the same tools, everything, and you get it perfectly consistent.

771
01:03:29,966 --> 01:03:31,824
现在，创建技能有三种方法。
Now, there are three ways to create a skill.

772
01:03:32,014 --> 01:03:35,024
第一种就是简单地向 Claude 进行描述。
Number one is to just simply describe it to Claude.

773
01:03:35,214 --> 01:03:42,144
你可以告诉 Claude 你想自动化什么，它会向你提问并为你构建这个技能。然后它还可以帮你运行测试。
So you can tell Claude what you want automated, it'll ask you questions and it will build the skill for you. And then it can also run the tests for you.

774
01:03:42,224 --> 01:03:45,904
这样你就可以给这个技能输入内容，并命令它执行该技能。
So you can give the skill an input, you can tell it to execute that skill.

775
01:03:45,998 --> 01:03:47,824
这种方法最适合处理新想法。
And this is best for new ideas.

776
01:03:48,014 --> 01:03:51,824
第二种方法是对 Claude 已经完成的操作进行逆向工程。
The second way is to reverse engineer something that Claude has already done.

777
01:03:51,984 --> 01:03:58,464
也就是说，你先通过正常的提示词工程获取到你想要的输出，经过一个过程，也就是和 Claude 进行一次普通的对话，
So you get the output that you want first by just prompting normally, going through a process, going through a normal conversation with Claude,

778
01:03:58,574 --> 01:04:03,344
然后你只需说一句简单的话：做一个能完全执行我们刚才操作的技能。
and then you say something as simple as make a skill that does exactly what we just did.

779
01:04:03,534 --> 01:04:11,824
这种方法最适合在你已经有成熟结果、且通过与 Claude 进行普通对话就获得了良好结果，并想将其转化为可重复过程的情况。
And this is best for if you have proven results and you got a good result with Claude just chatting with it normally, and you want to turn that into a repeatable process.

780
01:04:12,110 --> 01:04:17,504
第三种创建技能的方法是直接上传别人已经创建好的技能。
And then the third way to create a skill is to actually upload a skill that someone else has already created.

781
01:04:17,678 --> 01:04:22,704
如果你想创建强大的技能，我建议你获取我们的免费资源：DBS 框架技能。
If you want to create powerful skills, then I recommend getting our free resource, the DBS framework skill.

782
01:04:22,798 --> 01:04:28,704
这是我的兄弟 Drake 创建的，我将详细解释为什么它是在 Claude 中创建技能的最佳方式。
My brother Drake created this, and I'm going to explain exactly why it's the best way to create skills inside of Claude.

783
01:04:28,944 --> 01:04:32,464
什么是 DBS 框架？这个技能是什么？它对你有什么重要意义？
What is the DBS framework? What is this skill and why does it matter to you?

784
01:04:32,654 --> 01:04:37,824
DBS 中的 D 代表方向，这些是存在于 skill.md 文件中的指令。
The D in DBS stands for direction, and these are the instructions that live in the skill.md.

785
01:04:37,904 --> 01:04:41,744
这是该技能的名称、描述以及逐步执行的工作流。
This is the name and the description and the step-by-step workflow of the skill.

786
01:04:41,966 --> 01:04:44,384
你还可以在这里加入一些规则和准则。
And you also sprinkle in rules and guidelines here.

787
01:04:44,590 --> 01:04:46,372
接下来是 B，它代表蓝图。
Then we have B, which stands for blueprints.

788
01:04:46,464 --> 01:04:50,948
这些是示例、参考和指导，能帮助定制你的输出内容。
These are examples, references, and guidance that's going to help tailor your outputs.

789
01:04:51,182 --> 01:04:54,864
你可以把这些看作是让你的技能变得更强大的相关资源。
Think of these as the relevant resources that are going to make your skill more powerful.

790
01:04:55,054 --> 01:04:58,944
最后，我最喜欢的部分是解决方案，这会让你的技能更具动态性。
Finally, my favorite part is solutions, and this makes your skills more kinetic.

791
01:04:59,024 --> 01:05:04,384
你可以把它看作是可以存在于技能中并反复使用的计算机程序。
And you can think of this as computer programs that can live inside of your skill and be used again and again.

792
01:05:04,622 --> 01:05:12,544
如果有些内容是 Claude 平常无法很好处理的，你可以让它帮你写一段脚本或代码
